# Redirects for Cloudflare Pages — the replacement for the `return 301` locations in
# nginx/indianinprague.conf. Copied into dist/ by scripts/build-dist.mjs; Pages reads it
# from the deployment root and does not serve it.
#
# Format: <from> <to> <status>. Limits: 2,000 static + 100 dynamic rules.
#
# The site moved to EXTENSIONLESS URLs on 16 Aug 2026 (wrangler.jsonc:
# html_handling "auto-trailing-slash"). /wardrobe is the real URL; wardrobe.html is only a
# filename on disk. The asset server already serves / from index.html and already redirects
# the .html form, so no rewrite is needed for the homepage.
#
# The .html rules below exist anyway, and they matter. Left to itself the asset server sends
# /wardrobe.html to /wardrobe with a **307 Temporary** — measured. Every one of these URLs
# has been indexed for months and is what external links point at, and a temporary redirect
# tells Google the old URL is still the right one, which is the opposite of the truth. These
# rules answer 301 Permanent instead, so ranking consolidates onto the new URL. They are
# matched before the built-in behaviour.

# shop.html became wardrobe.html when the top nav went to five modules and the word "shop"
# left the visitor-facing site. It was the most linked and best indexed page here, so the
# old path stays alive permanently. 301 and not 302: the move is permanent, and only a 301
# passes the accumulated ranking to the new URL. Both forms, because both resolved before.
/shop.html                                /wardrobe                         301
/shop                                     /wardrobe                         301

/index.html                               /                                 301
/wardrobe.html                            /wardrobe                         301
/spirituality.html                        /spirituality                     301
/diaries.html                             /diaries                          301

# /restaurants and /article-contemporary-indian-wear were FOLDED INTO /diaries on
# 17 Aug 2026. Both pages are deleted; their content is inline on the Diaries under the
# category it belongs to, and every anchor they used (#annamalai, #indelicious, #dosa-dosa,
# #pastva, #palo-verde, #vegan) is an anchor on that page.
#
# 301 and not 302 for the usual reason — the move is permanent and only a 301 passes the
# accumulated ranking on. /restaurants is the most valuable URL involved: it held the position
# for the Prague Indian-restaurant searches and five Review nodes of structured data. Both the
# reviews and the schema were carried over to /diaries rather than dropped, which is what
# makes this survivable rather than simply lossy.
#
# The fragment is not the server's business and does not need a rule: a browser reapplies it
# to the redirect target, so /restaurants#annamalai arrives at /diaries#annamalai on its own.
/restaurants                              /diaries#food                     301
/restaurants.html                         /diaries#food                     301
/article-contemporary-indian-wear         /diaries/contemporary-indian-wear  301
/article-contemporary-indian-wear.html    /diaries/contemporary-indian-wear  301

# Every post got a page of its own on 17 Aug 2026 (see scripts/build-diaries.mjs). The
# redirect above now lands on the post itself rather than on an anchor in a wall of text,
# which is a better destination than it had a day ago.
#
# The one-day-old /diaries#annamalai style of link cannot be redirected here — a fragment
# never reaches the server — so the index keeps id="<post-id>" on every card. Such a link
# scrolls to the card for that post, which links to the post. Nobody arrives nowhere.
#
# /restaurants#annamalai therefore still works too: it 301s to /diaries, the browser
# reapplies #annamalai, and the card is there.

# THE SHELVES MOVED UNDER /wardrobe ON 21 AUG 2026.
#
# /wardrobe was already the storefront and the shelves were siblings of it — /clothes,
# /jewellery, /books — which said, structurally, that they were separate things. They are
# not: they are what is inside the wardrobe. With a second vendor's catalogue arriving the
# distinction stopped being cosmetic, because every new shelf would have had to claim
# another top-level path.
#
# 301 and not 302, for the same reason as every rule above: the move is permanent, these
# URLs have been indexed for months, and only a 301 passes the accumulated ranking on.
#
# Two shelves also changed name. /ritual-objects is /wardrobe/meditation — the shelf grew
# from 11 items to the largest one on the site, and "ritual objects" described the brass
# but not the malas, incense or deities. /more is /wardrobe/others, which is what a
# catch-all should be called.
/clothes                                  /wardrobe/fashion                 301
/clothes.html                             /wardrobe/fashion                 301
/jewellery                                /wardrobe/jewellery               301
/jewellery.html                           /wardrobe/jewellery               301
/home-decor                               /wardrobe/home-decor              301
/home-decor.html                          /wardrobe/home-decor              301
/ritual-objects                           /wardrobe/meditation              301
/ritual-objects.html                      /wardrobe/meditation              301
/books                                    /wardrobe/books                   301
/books.html                               /wardrobe/books                   301
/more                                     /wardrobe/others                  301
/more.html                                /wardrobe/others                  301
/sold                                     /wardrobe/sold                    301
/sold.html                                /wardrobe/sold                    301
